{"key":"nlp-basics-u4-04","seriesId":"nlp-basics","episode":"u4-04","title":"LSTMs: Remembering What Matters","fps":30,"duration":199.006,"durationInFrames":5970,"video":{"width":1920,"height":1080,"burnCaptions":true,"brand":"learnvi.in"},"badge":["UNIT 4 · LESSON 4","LSTMS"],"series":{"title":"NLP, Simply Explained","subtitle":"University NLP, one idea at a time, no heavy maths","runningPrompt":"","stops":[{"id":"u1-01","number":1,"name":"The Stages of NLP: From Letters to Meaning","stamp":"THE STAGES OF NLP: FROM LETTERS TO MEANING","topic":""},{"id":"u1-02","number":2,"name":"Tokenization: How Text Becomes Pieces","stamp":"TOKENIZATION: HOW TEXT BECOMES PIECES","topic":""},{"id":"u1-03","number":3,"name":"Text Classification: Teaching Computers to Sort Text","stamp":"TEXT CLASSIFICATION: TEACHING COMPUTERS TO SORT TEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u1-04","number":4,"name":"Language Models: Guessing the Next Word","stamp":"LANGUAGE MODELS: GUESSING THE NEXT WORD","topic":""},{"id":"u2-01","number":5,"name":"Morphology: The Building Blocks Inside Words","stamp":"MORPHOLOGY: THE BUILDING BLOCKS INSIDE WORDS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-02","number":6,"name":"Part-of-Speech Tagging: Is It a Noun or a Verb?","stamp":"PART-OF-SPEECH TAGGING: IS IT A NOUN OR A VERB?","topic":""},{"id":"u2-03","number":7,"name":"Chunking: Grouping Words into Phrases","stamp":"CHUNKING: GROUPING WORDS INTO PHRASES","topic":""},{"id":"u2-04","number":8,"name":"Generative vs Discriminative Models","stamp":"GENERATIVE VS DISCRIMINATIVE MODELS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-05","number":9,"name":"Hidden Markov Models, Intuitively","stamp":"HIDDEN MARKOV MODELS, INTUITIVELY","topic":""},{"id":"u2-06","number":10,"name":"Conditional Random Fields, Intuitively","stamp":"CONDITIONAL RANDOM FIELDS, INTUITIVELY","topic":""},{"id":"u3-01","number":11,"name":"Constituency Parsing: Sentences as Trees","stamp":"CONSTITUENCY PARSING: SENTENCES AS TREES","topic":""},{"id":"u3-02","number":12,"name":"Dependency Parsing: Who Did What to Whom","stamp":"DEPENDENCY PARSING: WHO DID WHAT TO WHOM","topic":""},{"id":"u3-03","number":13,"name":"Transition-Based Parsing: Building Trees Step by Step","stamp":"TRANSITION-BASED PARSING: BUILDING TREES STEP BY STEP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-01","number":14,"name":"Word Vectors: Giving Words a Place on a Map","stamp":"WORD VECTORS: GIVING WORDS A PLACE ON A MAP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-02","number":15,"name":"Word2Vec: Learning Word Vectors from Context","stamp":"WORD2VEC: LEARNING WORD VECTORS FROM CONTEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u4-03","number":16,"name":"Recurrent Neural Networks: Reading with Memory","stamp":"RECURRENT NEURAL NETWORKS: READING WITH MEMORY","topic":""},{"id":"u4-04","number":17,"name":"LSTMs: Remembering What Matters","stamp":"LSTMS: REMEMBERING WHAT MATTERS","topic":""},{"id":"u5-01","number":18,"name":"Contextual Embeddings and ELMo","stamp":"CONTEXTUAL EMBEDDINGS AND ELMO","topic":""},{"id":"u5-02","number":19,"name":"BERT: Reading in Both Directions","stamp":"BERT: READING IN BOTH DIRECTIONS","topic":""}]},"stop":{"number":17,"name":"LSTMs: Remembering What Matters","stamp":"LSTMS: REMEMBERING WHAT MATTERS"},"shorts":{"width":1080,"height":1920,"maxSeconds":60,"cta":"Full lesson: NLP, Simply Explained · Unit 4"},"thumbnail":{"headline":"How AI learned to remember","big":"forget · input · output"},"segments":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","component":"TitleCard","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c01","start":0.6,"end":7.127,"marks":{},"text":"Welcome back to NLP, Simply Explained. This is unit 4, lesson 4: LSTM networks.","words":[{"w":"Welcome","start":0.6},{"w":"back","start":1.08},{"w":"to","start":1.427},{"w":"NLP,","start":1.773},{"w":"Simply","start":2.12},{"w":"Explained.","start":2.76},{"w":"This","start":3.56},{"w":"is","start":3.84},{"w":"unit","start":4.04},{"w":"4,","start":4.52},{"w":"lesson","start":5},{"w":"4:","start":5.48},{"w":"LSTM","start":5.96},{"w":"networks.","start":6.44}]},{"id":"c02","start":7.527,"end":15.293,"marks":{},"text":"Last time, plain RNNs forgot the start of long sentences. Today's network was designed to fix exactly that.","words":[{"w":"Last","start":7.527},{"w":"time,","start":7.927},{"w":"plain","start":8.567},{"w":"RNNs","start":9.207},{"w":"forgot","start":9.847},{"w":"the","start":10.207},{"w":"start","start":10.407},{"w":"of","start":10.727},{"w":"long","start":10.887},{"w":"sentences.","start":11.207},{"w":"Today's","start":12.027},{"w":"network","start":12.847},{"w":"was","start":13.367},{"w":"designed","start":13.527},{"w":"to","start":13.967},{"w":"fix","start":14.127},{"w":"exactly","start":14.447},{"w":"that.","start":15.047}]}],"title":"Welcome","shortTitle":"Welcome","props":{"kicker":"Unit 4 · Lesson 4","title":"LSTMs","subtitle":"Remembering what matters"},"start":0.6,"end":15.293,"startFrame":0,"durationInFrames":486},{"id":"idea","kind":"core","component":"BigIdea","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c03","start":16.2,"end":25.247,"marks":{},"text":"Here's the idea. An LSTM keeps a separate, protected memory, and uses little gates to decide what to keep, what to forget, and what to use.","words":[{"w":"Here's","start":16.2},{"w":"the","start":16.56},{"w":"idea.","start":16.76},{"w":"An","start":17.4},{"w":"LSTM","start":18.04},{"w":"keeps","start":18.68},{"w":"a","start":18.96},{"w":"separate,","start":19.12},{"w":"protected","start":19.6},{"w":"memory,","start":20.2},{"w":"and","start":20.68},{"w":"uses","start":20.92},{"w":"little","start":21.36},{"w":"gates","start":21.64},{"w":"to","start":21.96},{"w":"decide","start":22.08},{"w":"what","start":22.52},{"w":"to","start":22.72},{"w":"keep,","start":22.88},{"w":"what","start":23.28},{"w":"to","start":23.48},{"w":"forget,","start":23.68},{"w":"and","start":24.16},{"w":"what","start":24.36},{"w":"to","start":24.6},{"w":"use.","start":24.8}]}],"title":"The big idea","shortTitle":"The big idea","props":{"kicker":"Key idea","text":"An LSTM keeps a protected memory, and uses gates to decide what to keep, forget and use.","highlight":["gates"]},"start":16.2,"end":25.247,"startFrame":486,"durationInFrames":299},{"id":"lstm","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c04","start":26.167,"end":36.543,"marks":{},"text":"LSTM stands for long short-term memory. It's an RNN with a separate memory cell, and gates that control what gets written into it, kept in it, and read from it.","words":[{"w":"LSTM","start":26.587},{"w":"stands","start":27.007},{"w":"for","start":27.367},{"w":"long","start":27.647},{"w":"short-term","start":28.147},{"w":"memory.","start":28.647},{"w":"It's","start":29.287},{"w":"an","start":29.7},{"w":"RNN","start":30.114},{"w":"with","start":30.527},{"w":"a","start":30.687},{"w":"separate","start":30.767},{"w":"memory","start":31.207},{"w":"cell,","start":31.647},{"w":"and","start":32.087},{"w":"gates","start":32.327},{"w":"that","start":32.727},{"w":"control","start":32.927},{"w":"what","start":33.447},{"w":"gets","start":33.607},{"w":"written","start":33.887},{"w":"into","start":34.207},{"w":"it,","start":34.447},{"w":"kept","start":34.727},{"w":"in","start":35.127},{"w":"it,","start":35.287},{"w":"and","start":35.527},{"w":"read","start":35.727},{"w":"from","start":36.087},{"w":"it.","start":36.327}]},{"id":"c05","start":36.943,"end":42.734,"marks":{},"text":"In \"the keys that I left on the table are missing\", it can hold on to \"keys\" until it reaches \"are\".","words":[{"w":"In","start":36.943},{"w":"\"the","start":37.183},{"w":"keys","start":37.383},{"w":"that","start":37.783},{"w":"I","start":37.943},{"w":"left","start":38.143},{"w":"on","start":38.343},{"w":"the","start":38.503},{"w":"table","start":38.623},{"w":"are","start":38.943},{"w":"missing\",","start":39.103},{"w":"it","start":39.743},{"w":"can","start":39.943},{"w":"hold","start":40.143},{"w":"on","start":40.463},{"w":"to","start":40.583},{"w":"\"keys\"","start":40.783},{"w":"until","start":41.343},{"w":"it","start":41.663},{"w":"reaches","start":41.863},{"w":"\"are\".","start":42.383}]},{"id":"c06","start":43.134,"end":51.116,"marks":{},"text":"Think of a notebook with a careful editor. The editor crosses out old notes, adds new ones, and chooses what to read aloud right now.","words":[{"w":"Think","start":43.134},{"w":"of","start":43.294},{"w":"a","start":43.414},{"w":"notebook","start":43.734},{"w":"with","start":44.054},{"w":"a","start":44.174},{"w":"careful","start":44.574},{"w":"editor.","start":44.974},{"w":"The","start":45.374},{"w":"editor","start":45.774},{"w":"crosses","start":46.174},{"w":"out","start":46.694},{"w":"old","start":46.894},{"w":"notes,","start":47.174},{"w":"adds","start":47.654},{"w":"new","start":48.134},{"w":"ones,","start":48.374},{"w":"and","start":48.734},{"w":"chooses","start":48.974},{"w":"what","start":49.494},{"w":"to","start":49.694},{"w":"read","start":49.854},{"w":"aloud","start":50.094},{"w":"right","start":50.574},{"w":"now.","start":50.814}]}],"title":"What is an LSTM?","shortTitle":"What is an LSTM?","props":{"kicker":"Definition","term":"LSTM","definition":"Long short-term memory: an RNN with a separate memory cell, and gates that control what gets written, kept and read.","example":"keys … are: “keys” is kept until “are”","analogy":"A notebook with a careful editor who crosses out, adds, and chooses what to read aloud."},"start":26.167,"end":51.116,"startFrame":785,"durationInFrames":776},{"id":"gates","kind":"core","component":"Steps","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c07","start":52.033,"end":54.391,"marks":{},"text":"There are three gates, each with one job.","words":[{"w":"There","start":52.033},{"w":"are","start":52.193},{"w":"three","start":52.353},{"w":"gates,","start":52.593},{"w":"each","start":53.113},{"w":"with","start":53.393},{"w":"one","start":53.633},{"w":"job.","start":53.913}]},{"id":"c08","start":54.791,"end":59.305,"marks":{},"text":"The forget gate decides what to erase from memory, because it's no longer needed.","words":[{"w":"The","start":54.791},{"w":"forget","start":54.911},{"w":"gate","start":55.311},{"w":"decides","start":55.631},{"w":"what","start":56.151},{"w":"to","start":56.351},{"w":"erase","start":56.471},{"w":"from","start":56.911},{"w":"memory,","start":57.111},{"w":"because","start":57.671},{"w":"it's","start":57.911},{"w":"no","start":58.271},{"w":"longer","start":58.511},{"w":"needed.","start":58.831}]},{"id":"c09","start":59.705,"end":64.859,"marks":{},"text":"The input gate decides what new information from this word is worth writing down.","words":[{"w":"The","start":59.705},{"w":"input","start":60.025},{"w":"gate","start":60.345},{"w":"decides","start":60.825},{"w":"what","start":61.465},{"w":"new","start":61.665},{"w":"information","start":61.865},{"w":"from","start":62.545},{"w":"this","start":62.745},{"w":"word","start":62.985},{"w":"is","start":63.265},{"w":"worth","start":63.545},{"w":"writing","start":64.005},{"w":"down.","start":64.465}]},{"id":"c10","start":65.259,"end":69.194,"marks":{},"text":"And the output gate decides which part of the memory to use right now.","words":[{"w":"And","start":65.259},{"w":"the","start":65.379},{"w":"output","start":65.539},{"w":"gate","start":66.059},{"w":"decides","start":66.499},{"w":"which","start":67.099},{"w":"part","start":67.299},{"w":"of","start":67.499},{"w":"the","start":67.579},{"w":"memory","start":67.699},{"w":"to","start":68.099},{"w":"use","start":68.299},{"w":"right","start":68.659},{"w":"now.","start":68.939}]}],"title":"Three gates","shortTitle":"The 3 gates that gave AI a memory","props":{"kicker":"The gates","title":"Three gates, three jobs","steps":[{"label":"Forget gate","detail":"what to erase from memory"},{"label":"Input gate","detail":"what new information to write"},{"label":"Output gate","detail":"what to use right now"}]},"start":52.033,"end":69.194,"startFrame":1561,"durationInFrames":542},{"id":"example","kind":"core","component":"Table","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c11","start":70.1,"end":73.652,"marks":{},"text":"Here's a simplified picture of the gates at work on our sentence.","words":[{"w":"Here's","start":70.1},{"w":"a","start":70.42},{"w":"simplified","start":70.54},{"w":"picture","start":71.26},{"w":"of","start":71.66},{"w":"the","start":71.74},{"w":"gates","start":71.9},{"w":"at","start":72.3},{"w":"work","start":72.5},{"w":"on","start":72.74},{"w":"our","start":72.9},{"w":"sentence.","start":73.1}]},{"id":"c12","start":74.052,"end":77.78,"marks":{},"text":"At \"keys\", the input gate writes a note: the subject is plural.","words":[{"w":"At","start":74.052},{"w":"\"keys\",","start":74.252},{"w":"the","start":74.692},{"w":"input","start":74.972},{"w":"gate","start":75.252},{"w":"writes","start":75.532},{"w":"a","start":75.852},{"w":"note:","start":75.972},{"w":"the","start":76.292},{"w":"subject","start":76.452},{"w":"is","start":77.052},{"w":"plural.","start":77.252}]},{"id":"c13","start":78.18,"end":83.673,"marks":{},"text":"Through \"that I left on the table\", the forget gate leaves that note alone, so it survives the detour.","words":[{"w":"Through","start":78.18},{"w":"\"that","start":78.54},{"w":"I","start":78.74},{"w":"left","start":78.94},{"w":"on","start":79.18},{"w":"the","start":79.34},{"w":"table\",","start":79.5},{"w":"the","start":79.94},{"w":"forget","start":80.14},{"w":"gate","start":80.58},{"w":"leaves","start":80.9},{"w":"that","start":81.22},{"w":"note","start":81.46},{"w":"alone,","start":81.74},{"w":"so","start":82.18},{"w":"it","start":82.34},{"w":"survives","start":82.5},{"w":"the","start":83.02},{"w":"detour.","start":83.18}]},{"id":"c14","start":84.073,"end":88.913,"marks":{},"text":"At \"are\", the output gate reads the note: plural subject, so the verb should be \"are\".","words":[{"w":"At","start":84.246},{"w":"\"are\",","start":84.42},{"w":"the","start":84.593},{"w":"output","start":84.793},{"w":"gate","start":85.193},{"w":"reads","start":85.513},{"w":"the","start":85.873},{"w":"note:","start":86.033},{"w":"plural","start":86.433},{"w":"subject,","start":86.993},{"w":"so","start":87.513},{"w":"the","start":87.753},{"w":"verb","start":87.993},{"w":"should","start":88.233},{"w":"be","start":88.46},{"w":"\"are\".","start":88.686}]}],"title":"Gates in action","shortTitle":"Gates in action","props":{"kicker":"Simplified","title":"“The keys that I left on the table are missing”","columns":["At the word…","The LSTM…"],"rows":[["keys","writes: subject is plural"],["that I left on the table","keeps that note, ignores the detour"],["are","reads it: plural, so “are”"]],"highlight":[{"row":2}]},"start":70.1,"end":88.913,"startFrame":2103,"durationInFrames":592},{"id":"vs","kind":"core","component":"Compare","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c15","start":89.833,"end":91.233,"marks":{},"text":"So what's really different?","words":[{"w":"So","start":89.833},{"w":"what's","start":89.993},{"w":"really","start":90.313},{"w":"different?","start":90.713}]},{"id":"c16","start":91.633,"end":98.74,"marks":{},"text":"A plain RNN has one memory that gets completely rewritten at every step, so long-range details fade away.","words":[{"w":"A","start":91.633},{"w":"plain","start":91.793},{"w":"RNN","start":92.313},{"w":"has","start":92.833},{"w":"one","start":93.033},{"w":"memory","start":93.273},{"w":"that","start":93.753},{"w":"gets","start":93.953},{"w":"completely","start":94.273},{"w":"rewritten","start":94.833},{"w":"at","start":95.393},{"w":"every","start":95.553},{"w":"step,","start":95.873},{"w":"so","start":96.393},{"w":"long-range","start":96.933},{"w":"details","start":97.473},{"w":"fade","start":98.033},{"w":"away.","start":98.393}]},{"id":"c17","start":99.14,"end":110.779,"marks":{},"text":"An LSTM changes its memory cell carefully, only where the gates allow. That protects important information, and it lets the learning signal travel much further back without vanishing.","words":[{"w":"An","start":99.487},{"w":"LSTM","start":99.833},{"w":"changes","start":100.18},{"w":"its","start":100.66},{"w":"memory","start":100.9},{"w":"cell","start":101.34},{"w":"carefully,","start":101.7},{"w":"only","start":102.5},{"w":"where","start":102.82},{"w":"the","start":102.98},{"w":"gates","start":103.18},{"w":"allow.","start":103.62},{"w":"That","start":104.26},{"w":"protects","start":104.66},{"w":"important","start":105.26},{"w":"information,","start":105.78},{"w":"and","start":106.58},{"w":"it","start":106.82},{"w":"lets","start":107.02},{"w":"the","start":107.3},{"w":"learning","start":107.46},{"w":"signal","start":107.9},{"w":"travel","start":108.38},{"w":"much","start":108.82},{"w":"further","start":109.06},{"w":"back","start":109.54},{"w":"without","start":109.82},{"w":"vanishing.","start":110.14}]}],"title":"RNN versus LSTM","shortTitle":"RNN versus LSTM","props":{"kicker":"The difference","title":"Plain RNN versus LSTM","columns":[{"title":"Plain RNN","items":["one memory, rewritten every step","long-range details fade away"],"tone":"bad"},{"title":"LSTM","items":["a memory cell, changed carefully","gates protect what matters"],"tone":"good"}],"verdict":{"text":"Gates let learning reach far back"}},"start":89.833,"end":110.779,"startFrame":2695,"durationInFrames":656},{"id":"bi","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c18","start":111.7,"end":126.406,"marks":{},"text":"One more trick: a bidirectional LSTM, or BiLSTM. It runs two LSTMs, one reading left to right, and one reading right to left. Together, every word gets to see what comes both before and after it.","words":[{"w":"One","start":111.7},{"w":"more","start":111.98},{"w":"trick:","start":112.26},{"w":"a","start":112.7},{"w":"bidirectional","start":113.02},{"w":"LSTM,","start":113.78},{"w":"or","start":114.54},{"w":"BiLSTM.","start":115.42},{"w":"It","start":116.3},{"w":"runs","start":116.66},{"w":"two","start":117.353},{"w":"LSTMs,","start":118.047},{"w":"one","start":118.74},{"w":"reading","start":119.06},{"w":"left","start":119.5},{"w":"to","start":119.74},{"w":"right,","start":119.94},{"w":"and","start":120.26},{"w":"one","start":120.5},{"w":"reading","start":120.74},{"w":"right","start":121.22},{"w":"to","start":121.5},{"w":"left.","start":121.78},{"w":"Together,","start":122.26},{"w":"every","start":123.02},{"w":"word","start":123.38},{"w":"gets","start":123.7},{"w":"to","start":124.02},{"w":"see","start":124.18},{"w":"what","start":124.38},{"w":"comes","start":124.58},{"w":"both","start":124.9},{"w":"before","start":125.22},{"w":"and","start":125.62},{"w":"after","start":125.86},{"w":"it.","start":126.18}]},{"id":"c19","start":126.806,"end":132.899,"marks":{},"text":"To understand \"bank\" in \"she sat on the bank of the river\", the words after it, \"of the river\", matter a lot.","words":[{"w":"To","start":126.806},{"w":"understand","start":127.006},{"w":"\"bank\"","start":127.419},{"w":"in","start":127.833},{"w":"\"she","start":128.246},{"w":"sat","start":128.446},{"w":"on","start":128.686},{"w":"the","start":128.806},{"w":"bank","start":128.926},{"w":"of","start":129.206},{"w":"the","start":129.286},{"w":"river\",","start":129.446},{"w":"the","start":129.926},{"w":"words","start":130.166},{"w":"after","start":130.606},{"w":"it,","start":130.926},{"w":"\"of","start":131.166},{"w":"the","start":131.286},{"w":"river\",","start":131.486},{"w":"matter","start":131.966},{"w":"a","start":132.326},{"w":"lot.","start":132.486}]},{"id":"c20","start":133.299,"end":137.246,"marks":{},"text":"It's like reading a sentence twice: once forwards, and once backwards.","words":[{"w":"It's","start":133.299},{"w":"like","start":133.499},{"w":"reading","start":133.659},{"w":"a","start":133.979},{"w":"sentence","start":134.099},{"w":"twice:","start":134.619},{"w":"once","start":135.179},{"w":"forwards,","start":135.539},{"w":"and","start":136.059},{"w":"once","start":136.299},{"w":"backwards.","start":136.659}]}],"title":"Reading both ways","shortTitle":"Reading both ways","props":{"kicker":"Bidirectional","term":"BiLSTM","definition":"Two LSTMs, one reading left to right and one right to left, so every word sees what comes before and after it.","example":"“bank” … “of the river”: the words after help","analogy":"Reading a sentence twice: once forwards, once backwards."},"start":111.7,"end":137.246,"startFrame":3351,"durationInFrames":794},{"id":"uses","kind":"core","component":"Bullets","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c21","start":138.167,"end":140.191,"marks":{},"text":"LSTMs had a big impact.","words":[{"w":"LSTMs","start":138.607},{"w":"had","start":139.047},{"w":"a","start":139.207},{"w":"big","start":139.327},{"w":"impact.","start":139.567}]},{"id":"c22","start":140.591,"end":145.305,"marks":{},"text":"For several years they powered machine translation, speech recognition, and tagging.","words":[{"w":"For","start":140.591},{"w":"several","start":140.751},{"w":"years","start":141.231},{"w":"they","start":141.471},{"w":"powered","start":141.711},{"w":"machine","start":142.031},{"w":"translation,","start":142.471},{"w":"speech","start":143.271},{"w":"recognition,","start":143.791},{"w":"and","start":144.511},{"w":"tagging.","start":144.751}]},{"id":"c23","start":145.705,"end":150.143,"marks":{},"text":"A simpler cousin, the GRU, does a similar job with just two gates.","words":[{"w":"A","start":145.705},{"w":"simpler","start":145.825},{"w":"cousin,","start":146.265},{"w":"the","start":146.745},{"w":"GRU,","start":147.065},{"w":"does","start":147.745},{"w":"a","start":148.025},{"w":"similar","start":148.145},{"w":"job","start":148.665},{"w":"with","start":148.985},{"w":"just","start":149.145},{"w":"two","start":149.385},{"w":"gates.","start":149.625}]},{"id":"c24","start":150.543,"end":156.056,"marks":{},"text":"In most tasks, they were later replaced by Transformers, which you'll meet with BERT in unit five.","words":[{"w":"In","start":150.543},{"w":"most","start":150.703},{"w":"tasks,","start":151.023},{"w":"they","start":151.583},{"w":"were","start":151.743},{"w":"later","start":151.903},{"w":"replaced","start":152.223},{"w":"by","start":152.703},{"w"