.","start":170.508}]}],"title":"Quick quiz","shortTitle":"Quick quiz: which gate forgets?","props":{"kicker":"Pause and predict","question":"Which LSTM gate decides what to erase from memory?","options":["Input gate","Forget gate","Output gate"],"answer":1,"explain":"The forget gate decides what's no longer needed."},"start":156.967,"end":170.991,"startFrame":4709,"durationInFrames":448},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","component":"Recap","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c28","start":171.9,"end":176.183,"marks":{},"text":"Let's recap. An LSTM keeps a separate, protected memory cell.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":171.9},{"w":"recap.","start":172.26},{"w":"An","start":172.847},{"w":"LSTM","start":173.433},{"w":"keeps","start":174.02},{"w":"a","start":174.26},{"w":"separate,","start":174.38},{"w":"protected","start":174.86},{"w":"memory","start":175.38},{"w":"cell.","start":175.82}]},{"id":"c29","start":176.583,"end":180.725,"marks":{},"text":"Three gates, forget, input and output, control what goes in and out.","words":[{"w":"Three","start":176.583},{"w":"gates,","start":176.863},{"w":"forget,","start":177.263},{"w":"input","start":177.723},{"w":"and","start":178.183},{"w":"output,","start":178.563},{"w":"control","start":178.943},{"w":"what","start":179.543},{"w":"goes","start":179.743},{"w":"in","start":180.063},{"w":"and","start":180.223},{"w":"out.","start":180.423}]},{"id":"c30","start":181.125,"end":185.459,"marks":{},"text":"That keeps long-range information alive, so it remembers \"keys\" until \"are\".","words":[{"w":"That","start":181.125},{"w":"keeps","start":181.285},{"w":"long-range","start":181.745},{"w":"information","start":182.205},{"w":"alive,","start":182.725},{"w":"so","start":183.245},{"w":"it","start":183.445},{"w":"remembers","start":183.605},{"w":"\"keys\"","start":184.165},{"w":"until","start":184.685},{"w":"\"are\".","start":185.072}]},{"id":"c31","start":185.859,"end":191.413,"marks":{},"text":"And a BiLSTM reads in both directions, so every word 